A||||25||pontiacs4me||why does it seem the fiero community is falling apart?||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||10-07-2001||07:38 PM||||It seems to me lately that the fiero world is slowly falling apart.  People are beginning to fight about stupid and trivial things, people are flaming others because they have nothing better to do, people are getting upset about it and leaving the forum.  All of us here love fieros.  In the real world we are far and few between, we all need to stick together no matter what.  There is no reason to fight over whether a certain car has power steering or not, that is just stupid.  When I first joined this forum the comraddery was so great here, people were so willing to help out, and im not saying that you all arent still, but lately some of the posts are just filled with flames, because they hold a grudge against the person posting the question.  If there is a person on the forum you dont care for, avoid their posts.  you dont need to humiliate them every chance you get, just to make yourself feel better.  Think of it this way, say you drive to your local grocery store in your prized fiero, and as you pull in you notice a nice fiero in the parking lot.  You decide to park next to it, just because.  As you are getting out of your car the owner of the other fiero is approaching his, and you two strike up a conversation.  You guys could talk for an hour about fieros, and you will probably get along great.  Why?  because there arent all that many fieros around anymore, and you two show common ground.  You both love fieros.  Well all of us here love fieros, why do some of us hate others?  For all you know that guy you met at the grocery store could be the guy you hate online, but why did you get along so well in the parking lot talking about fieros?  Come on people keep the fiero community tight like always, theres no reason to fight over trivial crap, were all in this hobby together, let it stay that way.  For each forum member you run off, thats another potential fiero you will see in a salvage yard someday.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||10-07-2001||07:41 PM||||AMEN||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-07-2001||07:56 PM||||I make a big distinction between what goes on in O/T and what happens elsewhere on the forum. there's even a big distinction as to what happens thread-thread. A while back, I slagged JohnnyK hardcore over a femminist issue. Did the same after some things about 9-11. Doesn't change the fact that If I know an answer to any of his questions (in potentia) that I won't answer 'em. Same with Edsb52. I scream bloody murder about him in one thread, and back him in the next.<P>C'mon people, it's a forum. Open discussion. shoes are thrown, sometimes. Doesn't mean we hate each other... No matter how vocal an argument gets, there is rarely any true animosity. Anyone want to disagree? Who still hates me?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So no, I don't think the communities coming apart. People are getting more vocal, yes. But is there anyone who is harboring any true long-term animosity towards another member specifically? Or are they like me, and say, "Hell! It's just the internet!"<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000003||Sage||10-07-2001||07:56 PM||||Pontiacs4me:<P>Well said.  You got my vote!<P>Have a good one!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||85 gt fiero||10-07-2001||08:09 PM||||Amen, one time while i was at the local meijers store and parked next to a nice 84 se bright red, really nice car, i got out of my 85 gt rally car and the lady said nice car what is it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">ahh...85 gt,oh who makes that, ahh.. pontiac, oh thats a fiero aint it, yeah same as yours, yah its my husbands car i dont like it much because its small, End of conversation i walked away, HeHeHe lady didnt even now what it was. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Oh Yah..the first thing she asked was if i had a liscene. Hummmm.... I think she was drunk.   HeHe.......||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||10-07-2001||10:55 PM||||I too have noticed this around here.<BR>It seems like there have been a few people that have come down hard on people for either asking a question or especially stating an opinion. This is especially true if the question or opinion doesn't jive with<BR>the flamers opinion or general opinion of the forum. I don't think there's anything wrong with disagreeing with someone but does it have to be done in such an angry or spiteful manner?<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||9
Z||000006||FieroMaster88||10-08-2001||12:28 PM||||I have noticed this also.  I don't know why people cant get along and always have to try to prove something to someone else!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I just try to stay out of the arguments because most of them are really stupid.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||10-08-2001||12:49 PM||||I think the problem has to do with the size of <B>this</B> community. When the forum only had a few hundred members, we were a close group because we needed each other's help desperately. There wasn't a lot of information and there weren't a lot of people to get this information from.<P>Now, this forum has grown to over 3000 members. Members come and go daily but there are at least over a 1000 different people actively participating in the discussions. This means that the information flow has grown tremendously, and people take that for granted. The result is a general "I don't need <B>your</B> help" attitude amongst some members and this will reflect in their postings.<P><B>My</B> problem is that people will blame it on the forum instead of the persons in question themselves. "I'm leaving this forum", "The forum has become hostile" are remarks I often read. Well, the <B>forum</B> hasn't changed (much). <B>My</B> attitude towards what is and isn't allowed here hasn't changed over the years. The forum has always been kind of self-regulating and that's how I want it to stay.<P>Relatively, the flamewars are a small percentage of the total number of posts. And if people would simply ignore them instead of throwing in their 2 cents whenever they feel like it, they would become even rarer.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||10-08-2001||12:59 PM||||Thank you Cliff... you have spoken.  And your words of wisdom ring true.<P>No matter what the topic is, when there are 1000 people together in one place- there is going to be some disagreement.  I don't necessarily feel that the Fiero community is falling apart, just some people are taking this whole thing a little too seriously.  No matter how you break it down, we are all still a bunch of people with an unusual car being our connecting interest.  Nothing more, nothing less.  There will always be differences among us- that's what makes the community great: diversity.  Don't let it take away from the forum.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Archie||10-08-2001||01:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>I too have noticed this around here.<BR>It seems like there have been a few people that have come down hard on people for either asking a question or especially stating an opinion. This is especially true if the question or opinion doesn't jive with<BR>the flamers opinion or general opinion of the forum. I don't think there's anything wrong with disagreeing with someone but does it have to be done in such an angry or spiteful manner?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dave, you don't know what you're talking about.... besides you are a bumb & I don't like your haircut.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfixit58||10-08-2001||01:48 PM||||We could all take a lesson from Archie. He must have skin as thick as an elephant. I've seen him take some licks that would send most people running but he's still here contributing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000011||ChopTop||10-08-2001||02:30 PM||||What I've noticed after being online for several years is that words have limitations, especially when you cannot hear or see the other person talking.  Tone, inflection, and body language play a important role in communicating with each other.  Add in the fact that the Internet allows people to remain anonymous and it becomes pretty easy for abuse and misunderstandings to occur.   However, I also believe we do a pretty good job of policing ourselves on here.  Yes a few people say some things on here that may be better off NOT said, and yes some people get their feelings hurt and leave the forum, which is sad.  But for the most part, the majority of us realize that there is a person on the other end of the keyboard, and choose our words accordingly.  I’ve have also read sincere apologies offered when posters have realized they may have hurt someone’s feelings or had their facts wrong, and that is a good thing.  This forum gives us an excellent venue to support each others interest in owing and maintaining our Fiero’s, and as our cars age we will need that knowledge and support from each other more than ever.  Let’s continue to work together folks, it sure beats the alternative.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fierowrecker||10-08-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>What I've noticed after being online for several years is that words have limitations, especially when you cannot hear or see the other person talking.  Tone, inflection, and body language play a important role in communicating with each other.  Add in the fact that the Internet allows people to remain anonymous and it becomes pretty easy for abuse and misunderstandings to occur.   However, I also believe we do a pretty good job of policing ourselves on here.  Yes a few people say some things on here that may be better off NOT said, and yes some people get their feelings hurt and leave the forum, which is sad.  But for the most part, the majority of us realize that there is a person on the other end of the keyboard, and choose our words accordingly.  I’ve have also read sincere apologies offered when posters have realized they may have hurt someone’s feelings or had their facts wrong, and that is a good thing.  This forum gives us an excellent venue to support each others interest in owing and maintaining our Fiero’s, and as our cars age we will need that knowledge and support from each other more than ever.  Let’s continue to work together folks, it sure beats the alternative.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well said CT!<BR>We all need to take a second look at a post we think is meant to hurt, when in fact, it may be a poor attempt at humor...<BR>I know I make poor jokes at times, and I do not ever mean to hurt anyones feelings, but others may not understand my intentions, which is to make everyone smile!!!<BR>Remember, it takes two to make the flames grow higher, and there are many topics I do NOT respond to as I know my OPINION will rub many the wrong way...<BR>But if you ever feel someone is out to flame you, back off and think of the many ways it could have been meant, as our first reaction may not be what the sender meant...<BR>It is not a mater of growing up, getting tough, or having a thick skin, but understanding what we may think a person said isn't nessisarily what they meant...<BR>BUT, if a person takes a dislike to you and starts to flame you, perhaps they misunderstood one of YOUR comments, now the shoe is on the other foot...<BR>OFTA!<BR>Boy! Did I get long winded!<BR>Sorry!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Doni Hagan||10-08-2001||10:44 PM||||If you disagree with someone on a point of principle, that's one thing. I've always believed that there is always a way of expressing an advesarial position in an adult and intelligent manner. I don't mind being disagreed with. But I do mind adolescent name calling and mean spiritedness. It's petty and unnecessary. As I was recently reminded (and rightly so) by a fellow member that's what e-mail and private conversations are for. As I tell my 16-year-old daughter, if you must act a fool at least do it behind closed doors where as few as possible will have to witness it. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jncomutt||10-08-2001||10:47 PM||||All opinions well said.  I got my first Fiero just after I turned 16 and you can say it wasn't exactly in the best position.  And whether or not it was a small issue or a big problem I needed to get worked out, you guys were always here to help me through it.  I thank everyone for this.  We can't let the disagreements between us bring down the forum as mentioned by this topic.  I love my Fiero, heck, I think I love this forum for giving me the opportunity to love my car.  All in all, as I smiled reading this post, I too realized there is no need for flame, and that we need to Keep the Fiero Tightness of our "unique" community alive.  <P>Not sure if its wordy but bein round for the time that I have, even though VERY short compared to others, has shown me that the fiero community is different and that we have a respect within us.  I don't want to get too like 'mushy' or 'brokendown', as one would say, about this but I appreciate everything everyone here has done for me and my car.||||reg||1
